1
00:00:01,200 --> 00:00:05,330
DIMNA: Kalila, do you think a tiny hare could ever beat a big, strong lion?

2
00:00:05,480 --> 00:00:08,450
KALILA: A hare? Against a lion? Impossible.

3
00:00:08,600 --> 00:00:11,470
DIMNA: Then sit down, brother. Let me tell you a story.

4
00:00:16,620 --> 00:00:26,870
Once upon a time, there was a green and peaceful forest. The deer drank from the cool stream, the fox slept in the sun, and a little hare hopped among the flowers.

5
00:00:31,670 --> 00:00:38,720
But one day, a huge lion came to the forest. He was strong, and he was hungry, and he was very, very proud.

6
00:00:38,870 --> 00:00:43,860
LION: I am the king of this forest! Everyone here belongs to ME!

7
00:00:44,510 --> 00:00:50,980
Every day he hunted, and every day the animals ran and hid. Nobody played by the stream anymore.

8
00:00:53,980 --> 00:00:58,470
DEER: We can't live like this. Every day we run, every day we are afraid.

9
00:00:58,620 --> 00:01:00,930
FOX: Maybe we should all move far away?

10
00:01:01,380 --> 00:01:06,910
OLD TORTOISE: This is our home, little ones. Let us go and talk to the lion.

11
00:01:09,310 --> 00:01:15,430
OLD TORTOISE: Great King, you do not need to hunt. Each day, one of us will come to you.

12
00:01:15,580 --> 00:01:22,200
LION: Hmm. No running, no chasing... I like it. But if anyone is late, I will eat you ALL!

13
00:01:22,750 --> 00:01:28,050
So every morning, the animals drew lots. And every day, one animal had to go.

14
00:01:30,850 --> 00:01:32,730
HARE: Oh no... today it's my turn.

15
00:01:34,280 --> 00:01:39,430
HARE: Wait. I may be small... but my brain is not! I have an idea. I'll go slowly. Very... slowly.

16
00:01:43,430 --> 00:01:47,620
LION: YOU! You're late, and you're tiny! Where is my lunch?!

17
00:01:47,770 --> 00:01:53,070
HARE: Oh, great King! They sent a big fat hare with me, for your lunch. But on the way, another lion stole him!

18
00:01:53,220 --> 00:01:57,710
LION: ANOTHER lion? In MY forest?! Show me where he is!

19
00:01:57,860 --> 00:02:02,020
HARE: He said he's the real king, and he's hiding in a deep well. Come, I'll show you!

20
00:02:03,420 --> 00:02:08,700
So the little hare led the big lion through the forest, all the way to an old, deep well.

21
00:02:12,500 --> 00:02:14,600
HARE: There he is, Your Majesty. Look!

22
00:02:14,750 --> 00:02:17,700
LION: You there! Get out of my forest!

23
00:02:19,050 --> 00:02:26,720
The lion roared. The lion in the water roared too. So, with a mighty leap, he jumped in to fight... his own reflection!

24
00:02:31,520 --> 00:02:33,320
HARE: Hooray! The forest is free!

25
00:02:33,770 --> 00:02:37,280
OLD TORTOISE: The smallest of us has saved us all.

26
00:02:40,080 --> 00:02:44,230
KALILA: Hmm. So the hare didn't win with strong legs, or sharp teeth...

27
00:02:44,380 --> 00:02:47,970
DIMNA: ...he won with his head! Wisdom is stronger than strength, brother.

28
00:02:48,120 --> 00:02:52,820
KALILA: And next time: a monkey, a tortoise, and a very tricky friendship.

